  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Demonstrating Circular and Biobased Housing in the Kenyan Market</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Easy Building Concepts B.V. (EBC) has developed a circular and climate-neutral housing system (for emerging economies) based on FSC-certified wood from sustainable forestry. The standardised and scalable building concept can provide a solution for the growing demand for affordable, sustainable and climate-proof housing. This concept can easily be tailored to local customs, needs and demand using local knowledge, labour and materials. This is what is demonstrated with this DHI demonstration project.ECB wants to demonstrate at Mlango Farm, an educational farm with a focus on the environment and sustainability, where a demonstration of an Easy Home as an example of sustainable and circular construction methods fits well. Here, in addition to demonstrating the technical quality of the concept, they want to show that setting up a well-functioning, local sustainable production chain for wooden houses is feasible and that one can build competitively compared to traditional construction concepts.Because sustainable forestry is still very limited in Kenya, sustainable certified wood from Uganda will be used for the time being.</narrative>
  </description>
